{"availability":"available","full":"alfonsoj-entwickler/caesar-cipher-app","name":"caesar-cipher-app","description":"In cryptography, a Caesar cipher, also known as Caesar's cipher, the shift cipher, Caesar's code, or Caesar shift, is one of the simplest and most widely known encryption techniques. It is a type of substitution cipher in which each letter in the plaintext is replaced by a letter some fixed number of positions down the alphabet.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-07-20T16:17:33Z","updated":"2026-09-24T19:39:41Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://caesar-cipher-app-sigma.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://caesar-cipher-app-sigma.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.411Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.411Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.411Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.411Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive, real-time cryptographic tool for exploring the classic Caesar shift cipher.","The Caesar Cipher App is an educational, web-based tool designed to demonstrate the fundamentals of classical substitution ciphers. In cryptography, the Caesar cipher (also known as the shift cipher or Caesar's code) operates by replacing each character in a plaintext message with a character shifted by a fixed number of positions down the character spectrum.","This application provides an intuitive dual-panel interface where users can type in either plaintext or ciphertext and watch real-time encryption and decryption take place as they tweak rotation values."],"features":["⚡ Real-Time Bidirectional Transformation: Automatically encrypt plaintext into ciphertext, or decrypt ciphertext back into plaintext instantaneously as you type.","🔄 Dynamic Shift Adjustment: Increment or decrement the rotation/shift factor on the fly; all output recalculates automatically.","📋 Clipboard Integration: Built-in copy and paste controls for both plain and cipher fields, complete with non-intrusive toast notifications powered by React Toastify.","🔤 Extended ASCII Support: Extends beyond standard 26-letter alphabetic rotation to handle a wider set of printable and extended ASCII characters using modular arithmetic.","🛡️ Input Validation & Limits: Max character guard (up to 600 characters) and safe clipboard truncation."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alfonsoj-entwickler/caesar-cipher-app/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6822a29c1ed8eb7ca25ef4d0d09f98646398d043788ee4227ae7142680e1783a","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.572Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.572Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interactive, real-time cryptographic tool for exploring the classic Caesar shift cipher.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alfonsoj-entwickler/caesar-cipher-app/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6822a29c1ed8eb7ca25ef4d0d09f98646398d043788ee4227ae7142680e1783a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alfonsoj-entwickler/caesar-cipher-app/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.573Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-24T19:39:41Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alfonsoj-entwickler/caesar-cipher-app/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:07.574Z","hash":"6822a29c1ed8eb7ca25ef4d0d09f98646398d043788ee4227ae7142680e1783a","originalBytes":6682,"storedBytes":6682,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cipher","caesar","character","npm","shift","react","rotation","run","app","application","plaintext","bash","characters","ciphertext","input","next","url","build","clipboard","code","copy","css","custom","decryption","dev","encryption","output","real-time","server","start","tailwind","action","ascii","base","buttons","caesar-cipher-app","check","clone","components","context","controls","deployment","development","dynamic","educational","